1
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:06,460
<i>Seiichi and the wounded Louise set off 
from Barbador Magic Academy.</i>

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,140
<i>After they arrived,</i>

3
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:15,130
<i>the Wimberg Kingdom and the Demon Kingdom 
successfully forged their alliance.</i>

4
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:19,240
<i>Meanwhile, back at Barbador Magic Academy,</i>

5
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:24,040
<i>Airin was acting somewhat suspiciously...</i>

6
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:27,330
Guess it's about time.

7
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:35,010
<i>This week, we're starting with what 
happened at Barbador Magic Academy</i>

8
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:37,890
<i>shortly after Seiichi left 
for the Wimberg Kingdom.</i>

9
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:43,230
Seiichi-sensei, take care.

10
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,320
Well, time to head back to the cafeteria.

11
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:49,510
That's all you ever do, glutton.

12
00:00:49,510 --> 00:00:52,300
All right, back to the classroom.

13
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:53,520
Time to head back.

14
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:55,620
I wish I could have gone with the boss man.

15
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:54,820
Time to eat more!

16
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:56,700
You <i>still</i> want to eat?

17
00:01:01,690 --> 00:01:05,410
What's wrong? You're usually much more lively.

18
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:08,550
You think Sei-chan will be okay?

19
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:10,550
It's Seiichi-kun we're talking about.

20
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:12,670
Of course he'll be fine.

21
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:14,300
I hope you're right.

22
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:17,550
I hope you're right.

23
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:22,180
Well, I'm going back to the classroom.

24
00:01:26,060 --> 00:01:30,320
Will everything really be all right, Sei-chan?

25
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:33,080
Without you here at the academy?

26
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:41,740
The Fruit of Evolution 2:

27
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:41,740
The Fruit of Evolution 2:

28
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:41,740
Before I Knew It, My Life Had It Made

29
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:41,740
Before I Knew It, My Life Had It Made

30
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:41,740
Before I Knew It, My Life Had It Made

31
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:09,100
Gempel the Doppelganger

32
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,430
<i>I'm Gempel the Doppelganger.</i>

33
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:12,860
<i>The man who would one day be known as one 
of the top four of the Great Devil Order.</i>

34
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:15,450
<i>Believe it or not, when I was a child,</i>

35
00:03:15,450 --> 00:03:19,580
<i>I grew up as an upper-class noble 
who didn't lack for anything.</i>

36
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:23,950
<i>But my heart never felt fulfilled.</i>

37
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:26,400
<i>I'd always realized it.</i>

38
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:32,520
<i>People weren't approaching me. 
They were only after my status as a noble.</i>

39
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:35,560
<i>Even my parents didn't show me any love.</i>

40
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:40,440
<i>I was nothing more than a tool to 
inherit and continue their lineage.</i>

41
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:44,390
<i>No one paid attention to my true face.</i>

42
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:48,900
<i>The moment I fell into despair over that 
was the moment I lost my face.</i>

43
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:52,120
Airin? What are you doing?

44
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:54,680
This is the men's bathroom.

45
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:57,590
<i>One of Hiiragi Seiichi's students?</i>

46
00:03:57,590 --> 00:03:58,690
<i>Perfect timing.</i>

47
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:00,710
What are you doing here?

48
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:03,330
I came here to crush you two.

49
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:05,600
To make Sei-chan feel despair.

50
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,310
Sei-chan? You mean Seiichi-sensei?

51
00:04:08,310 --> 00:04:10,660
Airin! What in the world is wrong with you?!

52
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:12,560
Here I go!

53
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:15,600
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

54
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,930
Doppelganger!

55
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:18,940
S-So bright!

56
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:21,570
This is what I'm doing!

57
00:04:21,570 --> 00:04:23,530
S-Saria-san?

58
00:04:24,990 --> 00:04:26,220
Transformation magic?

59
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:29,490
Baird's got you beat in terms of power.

60
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:32,080
I'm not so sure about that.

61
00:04:36,370 --> 00:04:37,580
She transformed?!

62
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:39,180
Is that Airin's magic?!

63
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:41,460
Whoa, man, what's going on?

64
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:45,630
By the way, I can also copy their specs.

65
00:04:53,770 --> 00:04:56,800
I didn't know Airin had 
an ability like this.

66
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,090
I'm...

67
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:00,690
...not Airin!

68
00:05:00,690 --> 00:05:03,100
My true identity is...

69
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:09,840
Gempel the Doppelganger, one of 
the Great Devil Order's top four!

70
00:05:07,990 --> 00:05:10,660
Gempel the Doppelganger

71
00:05:07,990 --> 00:05:10,660
Gempel the Doppelganger

72
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:13,120
Well? Surprised, aren't you?

73
00:05:13,510 --> 00:05:18,240
When Seiichi gets back, 
I'll execute you before his eyes.

74
00:05:19,410 --> 00:05:21,070
Hiiragi Seiichi.

75
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:25,470
I'll send everyone you 
cherish to the afterlife.

76
00:05:25,470 --> 00:05:26,940
Starting with...

77
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:40,520
<i>A member of Hiiragi Seiichi's 
army, Lulune the Donkey.</i>

78
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:43,290
<i>I'll bet he'll feel utter 
despair when he loses</i>

79
00:05:43,290 --> 00:05:45,740
<i>someone he's shared joys and sorrows with.</i>

80
00:05:46,350 --> 00:05:48,620
Your life is mine!

81
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:50,900
What?!

82
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:54,270
My food is mine!

83
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:57,210
I won't let anyone take it!

84
00:05:57,210 --> 00:06:00,860
Huh? Food? I wasn't after that.

85
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,670
<i>I was after your life!</i>

86
00:06:02,670 --> 00:06:04,920
Oh? Really?

87
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,170
Really.

88
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:07,570
Now that I look at you,

89
00:06:07,570 --> 00:06:09,780
you're Airin, from my class, right?

90
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:11,140
<i>This girl's an idiot!</i>

91
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:13,230
Sorry for surprising you.

92
00:06:13,230 --> 00:06:14,330
Don't worry about it.

93
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:17,100
So, why did you sneak up on me from behind?

94
00:06:17,610 --> 00:06:19,030
<i>Overlook that part!</i>

95
00:06:19,030 --> 00:06:20,690
<i>Not good! Is she onto me?!</i>

96
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:24,530
Are you...

97
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:29,250
hungry, by chance?

98
00:06:29,250 --> 00:06:30,360
Huh?

99
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:33,150
O-Oh, yes, I am!

100
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:37,660
I see.

101
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,040
Then here's my favorite!

102
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:41,350
Bakudan!

103
00:06:41,350 --> 00:06:45,170
Being hungry always makes you want 
to attack from behind, doesn't it?

104
00:06:46,830 --> 00:06:48,190
No, it doesn't.

105
00:06:48,840 --> 00:06:51,830
You're the one who tried to save my master.

106
00:06:51,830 --> 00:06:53,150
So have this as thanks.

107
00:06:53,610 --> 00:06:57,400
Besides, it's nice to share food and 
eat it together every now and then.

108
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:01,610
You're our friend, Airin.

109
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,330
I wouldn't normally do this for others.

110
00:07:05,330 --> 00:07:07,220
You're special.

111
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:11,530
<i>Friend...</i>

112
00:07:12,350 --> 00:07:14,350
Father, Mother.

113
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:15,820
Be quiet.

114
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:17,730
Today's meal is delicious.

115
00:07:17,730 --> 00:07:19,530
I'm so glad I made it.

116
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:36,430
It's good.

117
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,730
But why are you giving this to me?

118
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:42,580
Huh?

119
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:47,070
Well, partly to thank you 
for trying to save my master...

120
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:49,830
What? Is it stuck in your throat?

121
00:07:49,830 --> 00:07:52,860
N-No, it's just my allergies.

122
00:07:53,490 --> 00:07:56,770
But food also tastes better 
when you eat with someone.

123
00:07:56,770 --> 00:07:59,920
Now we're best friends!

124
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:05,860
<i>Best friends?!</i>

125
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:08,750
<i>You dumbass!</i>

126
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:10,850
Hey! Where are you going?!

127
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:12,220
<i>I also have empyema!</i>

128
00:08:25,810 --> 00:08:27,380
<i>I might have failed earlier,</i>

129
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:29,070
<i>but it won't go that way this time!</i>

130
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:33,140
<i>Oliga, I'll be taking your life.</i>

131
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:35,500
Oliga-chan!

132
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,780
Oh, Glutton.

133
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:40,870
<i>When she gets close, I'll snap her neck!</i>

134
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:45,000
This girl?!

135
00:08:45,490 --> 00:08:47,180
Here's an umbrella.

136
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:48,730
You didn't bring one, right?

137
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:53,440
You hold it, Lulune.

138
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,250
Since you're tall.

139
00:08:55,250 --> 00:08:56,720
S-Sure.

140
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:59,890
It's an upper-class noble! Get him!

141
00:09:01,050 --> 00:09:02,890
Hand over that damn umbrella!

142
00:09:02,890 --> 00:09:04,520
Hey! Give it back!

143
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:09,270
Gempel, I heard your family 
was stripped of its title.

144
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:12,430
All this time, you acted like 
you were so much better than us!

145
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,800
Why are you giving me an umbrella?

146
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:19,710
You'll get all wet yourself.

147
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,250
I'm fine.

148
00:09:21,250 --> 00:09:23,180
You may be a glutton,

149
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:26,040
but you're a good girl who's 
always sharing food with me.

150
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:29,590
Besides, you're my buddy.

151
00:09:34,670 --> 00:09:37,090
<i>I'm her buddy?!</i>

152
00:09:40,510 --> 00:09:43,720
<i>You dumbass!</i>

153
00:09:41,590 --> 00:09:44,620
Where are you going? You'll catch a cold.

154
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:47,510
<i>Idiots don't catch colds!</i>

155
00:09:50,930 --> 00:09:53,820
<i>I swear, every single one of them...</i>

156
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:57,580
<i>That's...</i>

157
00:09:58,690 --> 00:10:00,830
<i>Artoria the Calamity.</i>

158
00:10:01,490 --> 00:10:03,460
<i>This time, I won't fail.</i>

159
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:05,090
<i>I'll finish her for sure.</i>

160
00:10:05,090 --> 00:10:06,190
Doppelganger.

161
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:12,090
Using the man she loves the most,

162
00:10:12,090 --> 00:10:14,920
Hiiragi Seiichi.

163
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:17,010
Continued in the second half.

164
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:25,440
I want to be through 
the mountains by nightfall,

165
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,780
so let's deal with this quickly.

166
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:28,100
All right.

167
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:30,980
Then I'll go buy us some drinks.

168
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:32,450
Okay, thanks.

169
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:37,480
Huh?

170
00:10:44,990 --> 00:10:47,160
What's the matter?

171
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:53,340
Are you hurt anywhere?

172
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:59,840
N-No, I was just recalling the past.

173
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:03,370
It's nothing.

174
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:05,270
I'm fine, young lady.

175
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,080
Saria!

176
00:11:09,590 --> 00:11:11,870
I bought drinks, Seiichi.

177
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:15,560
<i>Hey, have I seen him before?</i>

178
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,130
<i>I found him.</i>

179
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:22,660
You're Seiichi-sensei from 
Barbador Magic Academy, right?

180
00:11:22,660 --> 00:11:24,390
How do you know me?

181
00:11:24,390 --> 00:11:26,690
You're famous!

182
00:11:26,690 --> 00:11:31,420
I heard you're so super strong that 
the king of Wimberg relies on you!

183
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:32,970
Huh? Really?

184
00:11:32,970 --> 00:11:34,510
Seiichi, you're amazing!

185
00:11:35,010 --> 00:11:37,420
I heard you're a real hero!

186
00:11:38,050 --> 00:11:41,090
What are you doing here all by yourself?

187
00:11:41,090 --> 00:11:42,110
Me?

188
00:11:42,110 --> 00:11:44,210
I'm on a journey.

189
00:11:44,210 --> 00:11:46,260
Searching for fun things to do.

190
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:48,750
Wow, how nice!

191
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:51,440
We're on our way back now.

192
00:11:51,770 --> 00:11:52,580
Hey...

193
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:55,860
Sensei, are you happy right now?

194
00:11:57,570 --> 00:12:00,930
He is! Right, Seiichi?

195
00:12:00,930 --> 00:12:02,530
Y-Yeah.

196
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,450
I'm jealous.

197
00:12:05,450 --> 00:12:07,370
Huh? What'd you say?

198
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:10,410
Nothing. See you, Seiichi-sensei.

199
00:12:10,410 --> 00:12:11,660
You're leaving?

200
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:14,780
It's okay.

201
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:17,640
We'll meet again for sure.

202
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,130
Bye-bye.

203
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:39,940
Hey, Ar!

204
00:12:41,190 --> 00:12:43,700
S-Seiichi?

205
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:45,620
Why are you here?

206
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:47,620
What about Wimberg? What about Saria?

207
00:12:48,270 --> 00:12:51,830
I came back all by myself 
because I wanted to see you alone.

208
00:12:53,130 --> 00:12:56,290
You're the only one I have 
eyes for right now, Ar.

209
00:12:56,290 --> 00:13:00,210
Wh-Where is this coming from?

210
00:13:00,610 --> 00:13:03,560
Ar, may I hug you?

211
00:13:04,130 --> 00:13:07,800
Wh-What are you saying?

212
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:11,420
S-Sei—

213
00:13:12,910 --> 00:13:14,640
<i>Got you.</i>

214
00:13:16,570 --> 00:13:20,860
What are you saying?!

215
00:13:21,270 --> 00:13:23,360
What has gotten into you?!

216
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:27,080
Seiichi!

217
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:30,420
Seiichi, are you okay?!

218
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:33,600
<i>Does this Seiichi guy go 
through this all the time?</i>

219
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:32,840
Sorry, it was force of habit!

220
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,820
B-But...

221
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:39,090
I really was worried about you back then.

222
00:13:42,730 --> 00:13:46,650
I'm truly glad you came back to life.

223
00:13:47,610 --> 00:13:50,600
<i>I'm the one who brought 
him back to life, though.</i>

224
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:52,670
I told you before, right?

225
00:13:52,670 --> 00:13:54,920
People call me the Calamity,

226
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:59,200
but you accepted everything 
about me, and I'm grateful for that.

227
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:04,030
So I want to accept everything about you, too.

228
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:06,820
Everything...

229
00:14:08,450 --> 00:14:15,400
<i>No one pays attention to my 
feelings, to my true face.</i>

230
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,220
Why?

231
00:14:21,350 --> 00:14:23,580
I-Isn't that obvious?

232
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:25,300
Because I—

233
00:14:25,890 --> 00:14:27,170
You?

234
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:29,760
Because I love you!

235
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:31,600
L-L-L...

236
00:14:35,850 --> 00:14:37,680
L-Love?

237
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:42,610
So, Seiichi, go ahead... and hug me!

238
00:14:46,130 --> 00:14:50,910
<i>Is Hiiragi Seiichi really such a good guy?!</i>

239
00:14:52,340 --> 00:14:53,870
H-Huh?

240
00:14:55,790 --> 00:14:56,900
Don't ignore me!

241
00:14:56,900 --> 00:14:58,080
Again?!

242
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:06,410
<i>Why do they all adore 
Hiiragi Seiichi so much?</i>

243
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:12,300
<i>I decided to spend some time 
as Seiichi in order to find out.</i>

244
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:14,720
Everyone did so well on their last quiz.

245
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:15,990
It's thanks to you, Sensei!

246
00:15:15,990 --> 00:15:18,100
Oh, no, that's not true.

247
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,820
Thank you so much.

248
00:15:24,550 --> 00:15:26,820
This is quite a feast!

249
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:31,470
It's nice to eat outdoors like this 
every once in a while.

250
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:33,490
The air is nice, too.

251
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:36,850
Yeah! This air is yummy!

252
00:15:36,850 --> 00:15:40,470
Lulune, you mean the sandwiches, not the air.

253
00:15:40,470 --> 00:15:41,940
Naturally!

254
00:15:44,430 --> 00:15:45,830
<i>Not good!</i>

255
00:15:45,830 --> 00:15:48,330
<i>I was planning to learn 
why they adore Seiichi,</i>

256
00:15:48,330 --> 00:15:52,630
<i>but I've started enjoying this school life!</i>

257
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:54,670
So, Principal...

258
00:15:54,670 --> 00:15:58,020
You wanted to discuss 
something with us, didn't you?

259
00:15:58,490 --> 00:16:00,630
Yes, actually.

260
00:16:00,630 --> 00:16:03,690
It's about the Great Devil Order.

261
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:08,270
You did say that the day 
of the final battle was close.

262
00:16:08,270 --> 00:16:09,560
That's right.

263
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:13,240
What I want to talk to you about is...

264
00:16:16,110 --> 00:16:17,910
What's this doing here?!

265
00:16:17,910 --> 00:16:22,680
Hmph. It's probably a monster that was 
awakened by the Great Devil's pulse.

266
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:29,130
This thing's strong!

267
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:32,050
Get away from it right now!

268
00:16:32,050 --> 00:16:33,750
I'd love to, but...

269
00:16:46,810 --> 00:16:48,110
Seiichi!

270
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:49,570
Onii-chan, you're amazing!

271
00:16:49,570 --> 00:16:52,490
You're so reliable, Master!

272
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:56,030
That makes it clear.

273
00:16:56,600 --> 00:17:01,650
To be honest, I've sensed an evil 
presence here at the academy lately,

274
00:17:01,650 --> 00:17:04,960
but I hadn't been able to locate it.

275
00:17:05,830 --> 00:17:10,570
He's an assassin sent 
by the Great Devil Order.

276
00:17:11,110 --> 00:17:12,900
What's wrong, Onii-chan?

277
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,970
You don't look happy.

278
00:17:14,970 --> 00:17:17,130
That's not true. I'm always with—

279
00:17:17,130 --> 00:17:19,610
Hold it right there!

280
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:25,560
Kannazuki Karen? Why are you here?

281
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:27,780
You might be able to deceive their eyes,

282
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:30,310
but you can't deceive my nose!

283
00:17:30,310 --> 00:17:32,980
That man isn't Seiichi-kun!

284
00:17:39,030 --> 00:17:40,450
Onii-chan?

285
00:17:40,450 --> 00:17:42,360
S-Seriously?

286
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:45,620
Do you... h-have any proof of that?

287
00:17:46,010 --> 00:17:47,600
I have evidence!

288
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,340
Airin?

289
00:17:54,630 --> 00:17:59,510
The one who approached Lulune 
several days ago was a fake Airin.

290
00:17:59,890 --> 00:18:03,950
I rescued the real one from 
the academy's chicken coop.

291
00:18:03,950 --> 00:18:07,020
Man, you really saved me from that one!

292
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:09,020
I don't know what happened,

293
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:12,180
but when I came to, I was with the chickens.

294
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:18,920
Even if you can copy his 
appearance and abilities,

295
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:23,160
you can't copy Seiichi-kun's 
fragrant body odor.

296
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:26,810
Then... who in the world are you?

297
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:31,210
Guess the cat's out of the bag now!

298
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:32,500
So bright!

299
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:38,490
I'm one of the Great Devil Order's top four,

300
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:40,470
Gempel the Doppelganger.

301
00:18:40,470 --> 00:18:44,640
One of the Great Devil Order's top four?!

302
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:47,590
You're right.

303
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:51,360
I used the chaos of the fight 
between Seiichi and the apostles

304
00:18:52,740 --> 00:18:55,410
to swap places with that lady there.

305
00:18:57,070 --> 00:18:59,030
Why would you do that?!

306
00:18:59,030 --> 00:19:03,900
Because I want to capture you all 
and eliminate you in front of Seiichi.

307
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:08,710
That's the best strategy for 
plunging him into the pit of despair!

308
00:19:08,710 --> 00:19:10,290
What?!

309
00:19:11,090 --> 00:19:15,090
At least, that was the plan before 
I became Seiichi and realized something.

310
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:21,630
I lived my entire life 
without being loved by anyone,

311
00:19:21,630 --> 00:19:25,100
so I never cared if anyone else died.

312
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:27,680
But now, I think I understand.

313
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:32,300
Losing the people precious 
to you is a very sad thing.

314
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:37,530
That's why I couldn't help saving you all.

315
00:19:39,270 --> 00:19:41,730
I'm such an idiot.

316
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:44,240
You...

317
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:52,610
From now on, I think I'll try to find 
someone to accept me like Seiichi did.

318
00:19:52,610 --> 00:19:54,680
Someone who will be fond of me.

319
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,760
At least, that's how I want to live.

320
00:19:57,350 --> 00:20:00,580
Though I doubt I'll ever measure up to him.

321
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:03,220
Later.

322
00:20:05,490 --> 00:20:07,540
You can do it.

323
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:10,490
I can smell that potential in you.

324
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:18,150
Thanks, lady with the keen nose.

325
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:24,110
Should we really just let him go?

326
00:20:24,110 --> 00:20:30,990
With his power, it would be 
a trivial matter to kill us all.

327
00:20:30,990 --> 00:20:32,830
Yet he didn't do that.

328
00:20:33,460 --> 00:20:36,860
So I want to believe in him.

329
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:40,610
I want to believe there's a ray of hope

330
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:44,420
for those who have made mistakes, as well.

331
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:55,460
Well, what should I do now?

332
00:21:02,910 --> 00:21:04,450
You, huh?

333
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:06,860
Perfect timing.

334
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:10,290
I'm leaving the Great Devil Order.

335
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:16,130
I don't care about all this despair 
and Great Devil stuff anymore.

336
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:20,670
So I'm going to find someone 
to love, who'll love m—

337
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,730
That boy was cute, wasn't he?

338
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:38,870
Yeah, he was.

339
00:21:40,110 --> 00:21:41,760
What's the matter?

340
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:42,820
Well...

341
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:46,380
I just feel like I've seen him 
somewhere before.

342
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:24,900
Everyone, the battle against 
the Great Devil Order is nigh!

343
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:26,750
So let's put our spirit into it!

344
00:23:26,750 --> 00:23:28,980
Yeah!

345
00:23:31,590 --> 00:23:34,420
Now, let's commence the operation.

346
00:23:35,990 --> 00:23:38,170
A murderer is on the loose 
in that crazy guild!

347
00:23:38,170 --> 00:23:39,670
The victim is the pacifier man!

348
00:23:39,670 --> 00:23:40,820
Wait, who's that?

349
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:42,510
Guscle and the others set out to resolve it,

350
00:23:42,510 --> 00:23:44,440
but wait, will I get to show up at all?!

351
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:46,450
Next time: "Vitor the Resonance."

352
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:47,730
Next Time
Victor the Resonance

353
00:23:46,450 --> 00:23:49,990
It's a sausage fest of perverted 
gentlemen showing off!

